---
// The real fingertip recording from the hackathon (902 camera frames of
// average red/green/blue over the flash, then a press-and-release), analysed
// here in the browser with the same steps as Vigil's server/vitals.py:
// settle, detrend, band-pass, spectral rate, beat detection, HRV, perfusion,
// breathing, then the refill fit. Nothing on this page is typed in by hand -
// every number is computed from the frames when the page runs.
import sample from "../../data/vigil-finger-sample.json";
---

<div class="interactive vigil" data-vigil>
  <script type="application/json" data-vigil-data set:html={JSON.stringify(sample)} />

  <p class="interactive__intro">
    This is the actual 30-second reading taken on a phone during the hackathon: a fingertip over
    the flash, the camera watching the glow. Each heartbeat pushes blood into the finger and the
    red channel dips. Press play to watch the pulse come out of that glow, and the numbers a nurse
    would see appear as the analysis runs.
  </p>

  <div class="vigil__panel">
    <div class="vigil__panel-head">
      <h3>Fingertip pulse</h3>
      <div class="vigil__controls" role="group" aria-label="Playback">
        <button type="button" class="vigil__btn" data-vigil-play>Play the recording</button>
        <button type="button" class="vigil__btn vigil__btn--ghost" data-vigil-speed aria-pressed="false">4x speed</button>
        <span class="vigil__clock" data-vigil-clock aria-live="off">0.0 s</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <canvas class="vigil__monitor" data-vigil-monitor height="170" aria-label="Pulse waveform from the fingertip recording"></canvas>
    <p class="vigil__status" data-vigil-status aria-live="polite">Camera settling, first two seconds are dropped.</p>
    <ul class="metric-row vigil__metrics" aria-label="Measured vitals">
      <li><span data-vigil-hr>–</span>Heart rate, bpm</li>
      <li><span data-vigil-rr>–</span>Breathing, /min</li>
      <li><span data-vigil-hrv>–</span>HRV (RMSSD), ms</li>
      <li><span data-vigil-pi>–</span>Perfusion index, %</li>
      <li><span data-vigil-sqi>–</span>Signal quality</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="vigil__panel">
    <div class="vigil__panel-head">
      <h3>Capillary refill</h3>
      <span class="vigil__crt" data-vigil-crt>–</span>
    </div>
    <svg class="vigil__refill" data-vigil-refill viewBox="0 0 600 180" role="img" aria-label="Red level during the press-and-release test"></svg>
    <p class="vigil__status" data-vigil-crt-note></p>
  </div>

  <div class="vigil__panel">
    <div class="vigil__panel-head">
      <h3>What the nurse board does with it</h3>
    </div>
    <p class="vigil__lead">
      The score is Vigil's real rule set: NEWS2 bands for heart and breathing rate, two points for
      a refill over two seconds, one for weak perfusion, two for a red-flag complaint, one for pain
      of eight or more, and trend since arrival. Type what a patient might type at check-in and
      watch the reasons change.
    </p>
    <div class="vigil__board">
      <div class="vigil__inputs">
        <label class="vigil__field">
          <span>What brings you in today?</span>
          <input type="text" value="headache since this morning" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" data-vigil-complaint />
        </label>
        <div class="vigil__chips" role="group" aria-label="Example complaints">
          {
            ["headache since this morning", "chest pain and sweaty", "can't breathe properly", "fever and confused", "fell, bleeding from my hand"].map((c) => (
              <button type="button" class="vigil__chip" data-vigil-example={c}>{c}</button>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <label class="vigil__field">
          <span>Pain: <strong data-vigil-pain-out>3</strong> / 10</span>
          <input type="range" min="0" max="10" step="1" value="3" data-vigil-pain />
        </label>
        <fieldset class="vigil__recheck">
          <legend>What if the 15-minute re-check read differently?</legend>
          <label class="vigil__field">
            <span>Heart rate <strong data-vigil-hr2-out>–</strong> bpm</span>
            <input type="range" min="40" max="150" step="1" value="72" data-vigil-hr2 disabled />
          </label>
          <label class="vigil__field">
            <span>Breathing <strong data-vigil-rr2-out>–</strong> /min</span>
            <input type="range" min="6" max="36" step="1" value="14" data-vigil-rr2 disabled />
          </label>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <div class="vigil__row" data-vigil-row>
        <div class="vigil__row-top">
          <span class="vigil__row-name">You</span>
          <span class="vigil__score"><strong data-vigil-score>–</strong> points</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="vigil__vitals" data-vigil-vitals></ul>
        <ul class="vigil__reasons" data-vigil-reasons><li class="vigil__muted">Waiting for the reading.</li></ul>
        <p class="vigil__flags" data-vigil-flags></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="interactive__note">
    One recording, one person, on a phone with no medical certification. Vigil is a reassessment
    aid for a nurse between checks, not a diagnostic: one camera wavelength means no oxygen
    saturation and no blood pressure. The server also shows a risk percentile from a logistic model
    trained on PhysioNet ICU data; that model is left out here so the page stays small. The
    re-check sliders are the only hypothetical inputs on this page, and they exist to show the
    trend rules.
  </p>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    const root = document.querySelector("[data-vigil]");
    if (!root) return;
    const DATA = JSON.parse(root.querySelector("[data-vigil-data]").textContent);

    /* ---------- numerics: the same operations as server/vitals.py ---------- */
    const mean = (a) => a.reduce((s, v) => s + v, 0) / a.length;
    const std = (a) => { const m = mean(a); return Math.sqrt(mean(a.map((v) => (v - m) * (v - m)))); };
    const clip = (v, lo, hi) => Math.min(hi, Math.max(lo, v));
    const percentile = (arr, p) => {
      const s = Array.from(arr).sort((x, y) => x - y);
      const idx = (p / 100) * (s.length - 1);
      const lo = Math.floor(idx), hi = Math.ceil(idx);
      return s[lo] + (s[hi] - s[lo]) * (idx - lo);
    };
    const median = (arr) => percentile(arr, 50);
    const diff = (a) => a.slice(1).map((v, i) => v - a[i]);

    // np.convolve(x, ones(w)/w, mode="same")
    function movAvgSame(x, w) {
      const n = x.length, out = new Float64Array(n), off = Math.floor((w - 1) / 2);
      const ps = new Float64Array(n + 1);
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) ps[i + 1] = ps[i] + x[i];
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const m = i + off, lo = Math.max(0, m - w + 1), hi = Math.min(n - 1, m);
        out[i] = (ps[hi + 1] - ps[lo]) / w;
      }
      return out;
    }
    // Direct DFT on the bins we keep. The recording is ~900 frames, so this is cheap.
    function dftBins(x, ks) {
      const n = x.length, re = new Float64Array(ks.length), im = new Float64Array(ks.length);
      for (let q = 0; q < ks.length; q++) {
        const w = (2 * Math.PI * ks[q]) / n; let r = 0, i = 0;
        for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) { const a = w * j; r += x[j] * Math.cos(a); i -= x[j] * Math.sin(a); }
        re[q] = r; im[q] = i;
      }
      return { re, im };
    }
    // rfft -> zero everything outside [lo, hi] Hz -> irfft
    function bandpass(x, fs, lo, hi) {
      const n = x.length, m = mean(x), xc = Array.from(x, (v) => v - m), ks = [];
      for (let k = 0; k <= Math.floor(n / 2); k++) { const fr = (k * fs) / n; if (!(fr < lo || fr > hi)) ks.push(k); }
      const { re, im } = dftBins(xc, ks), out = new Float64Array(n), half = n / 2;
      for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
        let s = 0;
        for (let q = 0; q < ks.length; q++) {
          const k = ks[q], a = (2 * Math.PI * k * j) / n, c = k === 0 || (n % 2 === 0 && k === half) ? 1 : 2;
          s += c * (re[q] * Math.cos(a) - im[q] * Math.sin(a));
        }
        out[j] = s / n;
      }
      return out;
    }
    // strongest frequency in (lo, hi) Hz of the Hann-windowed signal, and its height over the median bin
    function spectralPeak(x, fs, lo, hi) {
      const n = x.length;
      if (n < 8) return [null, 0];
      const m = mean(x), xw = Array.from(x, (v, i) => (v - m) * (0.5 - 0.5 * Math.cos((2 * Math.PI * i) / (n - 1))));
      const ks = [];
      for (let k = 0; k <= Math.floor(n / 2); k++) { const fr = (k * fs) / n; if (fr > lo && fr < hi) ks.push(k); }
      if (ks.length < 3) return [null, 0];
      const { re, im } = dftBins(xw, ks), P = Array.from(re, (r, q) => r * r + im[q] * im[q]);
      let best = 0; for (let q = 1; q < P.length; q++) if (P[q] > P[best]) best = q;
      return [(ks[best] * fs) / n, P[best] / (median(P) + 1e-12)];
    }
    // local maxima above zero, with a refractory gap that swallows the dicrotic notch
    function peaks(x, t, minGap) {
      const out = [];
      for (let i = 1; i < x.length - 1; i++) {
        if (!(x[i] > x[i - 1] && x[i] >= x[i + 1] && x[i] > 0)) continue;
        if (out.length && t[i] - t[out[out.length - 1]] < minGap) { if (x[i] > x[out[out.length - 1]]) out[out.length - 1] = i; }
        else out.push(i);
      }
      return out;
    }
    function interp(xs, xp, fp) {
      return xs.map((x) => {
        if (x <= xp[0]) return fp[0];
        if (x >= xp[xp.length - 1]) return fp[fp.length - 1];
        let i = 1; while (xp[i] < x) i++;
        const f = (x - xp[i - 1]) / (xp[i] - xp[i - 1]);
        return fp[i - 1] + f * (fp[i] - fp[i - 1]);
      });
    }
    // np.gradient(f, t) for unevenly spaced t
    function gradient(f, t) {
      const n = f.length, out = new Float64Array(n);
      out[0] = (f[1] - f[0]) / (t[1] - t[0]);
      out[n - 1] = (f[n - 1] - f[n - 2]) / (t[n - 1] - t[n - 2]);
      for (let i = 1; i < n - 1; i++) {
        const hs = t[i] - t[i - 1], hd = t[i + 1] - t[i];
        out[i] = (hs * hs * f[i + 1] + (hd * hd - hs * hs) * f[i] - hd * hd * f[i - 1]) / (hs * hd * (hd + hs));
      }
      return out;
    }

    function analyzePPG(frames) {
      const a = frames.slice().sort((p, q) => p[0] - q[0]);
      if (a.length < 100) return { ok: false, reason: "too few frames" };
      const t0 = a[0][0];
      let t = a.map((f) => f[0] - t0);
      const dur = t[t.length - 1], fs = t.length / Math.max(dur, 1e-6);
      const R = a.map((f) => f[1]), G = a.map((f) => f[2]);
      const torch = mean(R) > 120 && mean(G) < 60;
      let raw = torch ? R : G;
      const dc = mean(raw);
      if (torch && (dc < 60 || dc > 250)) return { ok: false, reason: "finger not covering the lens" };
      const keep = t.map((v) => v > 2.0);
      t = t.filter((_, i) => keep[i]); raw = raw.filter((_, i) => keep[i]);
      if (t.length < 100) return { ok: false, reason: "too short after settling" };
      const s = raw.map((v) => -v), w = Math.max(3, Math.floor(fs));
      const ma = movAvgSame(s, w), hp = s.map((v, i) => v - ma[i]);
      const bp = bandpass(hp, fs, 0.7, 3.0);
      const [fHr, snr] = spectralPeak(hp, fs, 0.7, 3.0);
      const expIbi = fHr ? 1 / fHr : 0.8;
      const pk = peaks(bp, t, 0.6 * expIbi);
      let ibi = pk.length > 2 ? diff(pk.map((i) => t[i])) : [];
      ibi = ibi.filter((v) => Math.abs(v - expIbi) < 0.25 * expIbi);
      const hrPk = ibi.length >= 5 ? 60 / median(ibi) : null;
      let hr = fHr ? fHr * 60 : null;
      if (hrPk !== null && hr !== null && Math.abs(hrPk - hr) < 0.1 * hr) hr = hrPk;
      const rmssd = ibi.length >= 6 ? Math.sqrt(mean(diff(ibi).map((v) => v * v))) * 1000 : null;
      const ac = percentile(bp, 95) - percentile(bp, 5);
      const pi = dc > 0 ? (ac / dc) * 100 : null;
      const cands = [];
      if (pk.length >= 8) {
        const tp = pk.map((i) => t[i]), amp = pk.map((i) => bp[i]), d = diff(tp), freq = d.concat([d[d.length - 1]]);
        const count = Math.ceil((tp[tp.length - 1] - tp[0]) / 0.25), tu = Array.from({ length: count }, (_, i) => tp[0] + i * 0.25);
        for (const series of [amp, freq]) {
          if (tu.length > 40) { const [f, q] = spectralPeak(interp(tu, tp, series), 4.0, 0.15, 0.6); if (f) cands.push([q, f * 60]); }
        }
      }
      { const [f, q] = spectralPeak(bandpass(hp, fs, 0.15, 0.6), fs, 0.15, 0.6); if (f) cands.push([q, f * 60]); }
      let rr = null;
      if (cands.length) { cands.sort((x, y) => y[0] - x[0]); rr = cands[0][1]; }
      const reg = ibi.length >= 5 ? clip(1 - (std(ibi) / mean(ibi)) * 2, 0, 1) : 0;
      const sqi = clip(Math.min(snr / 20, 1) * 0.6 + reg * 0.4, 0, 1);
      return {
        ok: hr !== null && sqi > 0.25, fs, t, bp, peaks: pk, beats: ibi.length,
        hr: hr ? Math.round(hr) : null, rr: rr ? Math.round(rr) : null,
        rmssd: rmssd ? Math.round(rmssd) : null, pi: pi ? Math.round(pi * 100) / 100 : null, sqi: Math.round(sqi * 100) / 100,
      };
    }

    function analyzeCRT(frames, releaseT) {
      const a = frames.slice().sort((p, q) => p[0] - q[0]);
      if (a.length < 100) return { ok: false, reason: "too few frames" };
      const t = a.map((f) => f[0]), R = a.map((f) => f[1]), n = t.length;
      const fs = n / Math.max(t[n - 1] - t[0], 1e-6);
      const sm = movAvgSame(R, Math.max(3, Math.floor(0.15 * fs)));
      let d = gradient(sm, t);
      if (releaseT != null) {
        const win = t.map((v) => v > releaseT - 1.5 && v < releaseT + 3.5);
        if (win.filter(Boolean).length > 5) d = d.map((v, i) => (win[i] ? v : 0));
      }
      let i0 = 0; for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) if (d[i] < d[i0]) i0 = i;
      if (d[i0] > -8.0) return { ok: false, reason: "no release detected", t, sm };
      const pre = t.map((v) => v >= t[i0] - 2.5 && v < t[i0]), post = t.map((v) => v >= t[i0] && v <= t[i0] + 6);
      const preIdx = [], postIdx = [];
      pre.forEach((b, i) => b && preIdx.push(i)); post.forEach((b, i) => b && postIdx.push(i));
      if (preIdx.length < 5 || postIdx.length < 20) return { ok: false, reason: "not enough data around release", t, sm };
      const y0 = percentile(preIdx.map((i) => sm[i]), 90);
      const tEnd = t[postIdx[postIdx.length - 1]];
      const yInf = median(postIdx.filter((i) => t[i] >= tEnd - 2.0).map((i) => sm[i]));
      const amp = y0 - yInf;
      if (amp < 12) return { ok: false, reason: "blanching too small", t, sm };
      const cand = preIdx.filter((i) => sm[i] >= y0 - 0.1 * amp);
      const on = cand.length ? cand[cand.length - 1] : i0, tOn = t[on];
      const segIdx = []; t.forEach((v, i) => v >= tOn && v <= tOn + 6 && segIdx.push(i));
      const ts = segIdx.map((i) => t[i] - tOn), ys = segIdx.map((i) => sm[i]);
      const thr90 = y0 - 0.9 * amp;
      let t90 = null; for (let i = 0; i < ys.length; i++) if (ys[i] <= thr90) { t90 = ts[i]; break; }
      const frac = ys.map((y) => (y - yInf) / amp);
      let end = frac.findIndex((v) => v <= 0.05); if (end < 0) end = frac.length;
      const fx = [], fy = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < end; i++) if (frac[i] > 0.05 && frac[i] < 0.95) { fx.push(ts[i]); fy.push(Math.log(frac[i])); }
      let tau = null;
      if (fx.length >= 5) {
        const mx = mean(fx), my = mean(fy);
        const slope = fx.reduce((s, x, i) => s + (x - mx) * (fy[i] - my), 0) / fx.reduce((s, x) => s + (x - mx) * (x - mx), 0);
        if (slope < 0 && 0.05 < -1 / slope && -1 / slope < 5) tau = -1 / slope;
      }
      return { ok: t90 !== null, t, sm, i0, tOn, y0, yInf, amp, thr90, t90, tau, releaseFrame: t[i0] };
    }

    /* ---------- scoring: score_patient and complaint_flags from vitals.py ---------- */
    const RED_FLAGS = {
      "chest pain": "chest pain", "chest pressure": "chest pain", "short of breath": "breathing", "shortness of breath": "breathing",
      "can't breathe": "breathing", "cant breathe": "breathing", "difficulty breathing": "breathing", "stroke": "stroke",
      "face droop": "stroke", "slurred": "stroke", "weakness one side": "stroke", "numb": "stroke",
      "pregnan": "pregnancy", "bleeding": "bleeding", "vomiting blood": "bleeding", "black stool": "bleeding",
      "fainted": "syncope", "passed out": "syncope", "unconscious": "syncope", "seizure": "seizure",
      "allergic": "anaphylaxis", "swelling throat": "anaphylaxis", "overdose": "overdose", "suicid": "psych",
      "infant": "infant", "baby": "infant", "fever": "fever", "confus": "confusion",
    };
    const SEVERE = new Set(["chest pain", "breathing", "stroke", "bleeding", "syncope", "seizure", "anaphylaxis", "overdose", "infant", "confusion"]);
    const complaintFlags = (text) => [...new Set(Object.keys(RED_FLAGS).filter((k) => (text || "").toLowerCase().includes(k)).map((k) => RED_FLAGS[k]))].sort();
    const newsHr = (hr) => (hr == null ? 0 : hr <= 40 ? 3 : hr <= 50 ? 1 : hr <= 90 ? 0 : hr <= 110 ? 1 : hr <= 130 ? 2 : 3);
    const newsRr = (rr) => (rr == null ? 0 : rr <= 8 ? 3 : rr <= 11 ? 1 : rr <= 20 ? 0 : rr <= 24 ? 2 : 3);

    function scorePatient(first, last, flags, pain) {
      const reasons = []; let score = 0;
      const h = newsHr(last.hr), r = newsRr(last.rr);
      if (h) reasons.push(`HR ${last.hr} (+${h})`);
      if (r) reasons.push(`RR ${last.rr} (+${r})`);
      score += h + r;
      if (first !== last && first.hr && last.hr && last.hr > 1.2 * first.hr) { score += 1; reasons.push(`HR up ${Math.round((last.hr / first.hr - 1) * 100)}% since arrival (+1)`); }
      if (first !== last && first.rr && last.rr && last.rr >= first.rr + 4) { score += 1; reasons.push(`RR up ${last.rr - first.rr} since arrival (+1)`); }
      if (last.crt != null && last.crt > 2.0) { score += 2; reasons.push(`capillary refill ${last.crt} s (+2)`); }
      if (last.pi != null && last.pi < 0.3) { score += 1; reasons.push("weak perfusion (+1)"); }
      for (const f of flags) if (SEVERE.has(f)) { score += 2; reasons.push(`complaint: ${f} (+2)`); }
      if (pain != null && pain >= 8) { score += 1; reasons.push(`pain ${pain}/10 (+1)`); }
      return { score, reasons };
    }

    /* ---------- elements ---------- */
    const $ = (sel) => root.querySelector(sel);
    const el = {
      play: $("[data-vigil-play]"), speed: $("[data-vigil-speed]"), clock: $("[data-vigil-clock]"), status: $("[data-vigil-status]"),
      canvas: $("[data-vigil-monitor]"), hr: $("[data-vigil-hr]"), rr: $("[data-vigil-rr]"), hrv: $("[data-vigil-hrv]"), pi: $("[data-vigil-pi]"), sqi: $("[data-vigil-sqi]"),
      crt: $("[data-vigil-crt]"), crtNote: $("[data-vigil-crt-note]"), refill: $("[data-vigil-refill]"),
      complaint: $("[data-vigil-complaint]"), pain: $("[data-vigil-pain]"), painOut: $("[data-vigil-pain-out]"),
      hr2: $("[data-vigil-hr2]"), hr2Out: $("[data-vigil-hr2-out]"), rr2: $("[data-vigil-rr2]"), rr2Out: $("[data-vigil-rr2-out]"),
      score: $("[data-vigil-score]"), vitals: $("[data-vigil-vitals]"), reasons: $("[data-vigil-reasons]"), flags: $("[data-vigil-flags]"), row: $("[data-vigil-row]"),
    };
    const cssVar = (name) => getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(name).trim();
    const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;

    /* ---------- the full analysis, once ---------- */
    const frames = DATA.frames, frameT0 = frames[0][0];
    const full = analyzePPG(frames);
    const crt = analyzeCRT(DATA.crt_frames, DATA.crt_release_t);
    const fmt = (v, d = 0) => (v == null ? "–" : v.toFixed(d));

    /* ---------- monitor ---------- */
    const WINDOW = 6; // seconds visible, like a bedside monitor sweep
    let playT = 0, playing = false, finished = false, speed = 1, lastTs = 0, raf = 0;
    const endT = full.t[full.t.length - 1];

    function drawMonitor() {
      const c = el.canvas, dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1, W = c.clientWidth, H = c.clientHeight;
      if (!W || !H) return;
      if (c.width !== Math.round(W * dpr) || c.height !== Math.round(H * dpr)) { c.width = Math.round(W * dpr); c.height = Math.round(H * dpr); }
      const g = c.getContext("2d"); g.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0); g.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      const accent = cssVar("--accent") || "#8a2438", line = cssVar("--line") || "#ddd8ce", faint = cssVar("--faint") || "#8b9698";
      g.strokeStyle = line; g.lineWidth = 1; g.beginPath();
      for (let s = 0; s <= WINDOW; s++) { const x = (s / WINDOW) * W; g.moveTo(x, 0); g.lineTo(x, H); }
      for (let k = 1; k < 4; k++) { const y = (k / 4) * H; g.moveTo(0, y); g.lineTo(W, y); }
      g.stroke();
      if (!playing && !finished && playT === 0) {
        g.fillStyle = faint; g.font = "600 13px Inter, system-ui, sans-serif"; g.textAlign = "center";
        g.fillText("Press play: 30 seconds of fingertip glow, 6 seconds on screen at a time.", W / 2, H / 2);
        return;
      }
      const tNow = finished ? endT : playT, tStart = Math.max(full.t[0], tNow - WINDOW);
      const bp = full.bp, t = full.t;
      let lo = Infinity, hi = -Infinity; for (const v of bp) { if (v < lo) lo = v; if (v > hi) hi = v; }
      const pad = 14, scale = (H - 2 * pad) / (hi - lo || 1), X = (tt) => ((tt - tStart) / WINDOW) * W, Y = (v) => H - pad - (v - lo) * scale;
      g.strokeStyle = accent; g.lineWidth = 2; g.lineJoin = "round"; g.beginPath(); let started = false;
      for (let i = 0; i < t.length; i++) {
        if (t[i] < tStart || t[i] > tNow) continue;
        const x = X(t[i]), y = Y(bp[i]);
        if (!started) { g.moveTo(x, y); started = true; } else g.lineTo(x, y);
      }
      g.stroke();
      g.fillStyle = accent;
      for (const i of full.peaks) { if (t[i] < tStart || t[i] > tNow) continue; g.beginPath(); g.arc(X(t[i]), Y(bp[i]) - 6, 2.5, 0, Math.PI * 2); g.fill(); }
      if (!finished) { g.strokeStyle = accent; g.lineWidth = 1; g.globalAlpha = 0.5; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(X(tNow), 0); g.lineTo(X(tNow), H); g.stroke(); g.globalAlpha = 1; }
    }

    function showMetrics(res, live) {
      el.hr.textContent = fmt(res.hr); el.rr.textContent = fmt(res.rr); el.hrv.textContent = fmt(res.rmssd);
      el.pi.textContent = fmt(res.pi, 2); el.sqi.textContent = res.sqi == null ? "–" : `${Math.round(res.sqi * 100)}%`;
      el.status.textContent = live
        ? `${res.beats} clean beats so far; estimates settle as more of the recording arrives.`
        : `${res.beats} clean beats in the recording; heart rate from the median beat interval, breathing from how the beats swell and shrink.`;
    }

    function partial(upTo) {
      const sub = frames.filter((f) => f[0] - frameT0 <= upTo);
      if (sub.length < 100) return;
      const r = analyzePPG(sub);
      if (r.hr != null) showMetrics(r, true);
      else el.status.textContent = "Listening for a pulse in the glow.";
    }

    let nextPartial = 6;
    function tick(ts) {
      if (!playing) return;
      const dt = ((ts - lastTs) / 1000) * speed; lastTs = ts;
      playT = Math.min(endT, playT + dt);
      el.clock.textContent = `${(playT + 2).toFixed(1)} s`;
      if (playT >= nextPartial) { partial(playT + 2); nextPartial += 1.5; }
      drawMonitor();
      if (playT >= endT) finish(); else raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    }
    function finish() {
      playing = false; finished = true; cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
      el.clock.textContent = `${(endT + 2).toFixed(1)} s`; el.play.textContent = "Play again";
      showMetrics(full, false); drawMonitor(); updateBoard(true);
    }
    el.play.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (playing) { playing = false; cancelAnimationFrame(raf); el.play.textContent = "Resume"; return; }
      if (finished) { finished = false; playT = 0; nextPartial = 6; ["hr", "rr", "hrv", "pi", "sqi"].forEach((k) => (el[k].textContent = "–")); }
      if (reduceMotion) { finish(); return; }
      playing = true; lastTs = performance.now(); el.play.textContent = "Pause";
      el.status.textContent = "Camera settling, first two seconds are dropped."; raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    });
    el.speed.addEventListener("click", () => { speed = speed === 1 ? 4 : 1; el.speed.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(speed === 4)); el.speed.textContent = speed === 4 ? "1x speed" : "4x speed"; });
    window.addEventListener("resize", drawMonitor);
    new MutationObserver(() => { drawMonitor(); drawRefill(); }).observe(document.documentElement, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ["data-theme"] });

    /* ---------- refill plot ---------- */
    function drawRefill() {
      const svg = el.refill, NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
      while (svg.firstChild) svg.removeChild(svg.firstChild);
      const accent = cssVar("--accent") || "#8a2438", line = cssVar("--line") || "#ddd8ce", faint = cssVar("--faint") || "#8b9698", ink = cssVar("--ink") || "#1d2528";
      const mk = (tag, attrs, text) => { const e = document.createElementNS(NS, tag); for (const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); if (text != null) e.textContent = text; svg.appendChild(e); return e; };
      if (!crt.t) return;
      const anchor = crt.ok ? crt.tOn : crt.t[Math.floor(crt.t.length / 2)];
      const tA = anchor - 3, tB = anchor + 6, W = 600, H = 180, padL = 40, padR = 16, padT = 18, padB = 26;
      const idx = []; crt.t.forEach((v, i) => v >= tA && v <= tB && idx.push(i));
      let lo = Infinity, hi = -Infinity; for (const i of idx) { if (crt.sm[i] < lo) lo = crt.sm[i]; if (crt.sm[i] > hi) hi = crt.sm[i]; }
      lo -= 3; hi += 3;
      const X = (tt) => padL + ((tt - tA) / (tB - tA)) * (W - padL - padR), Y = (v) => padT + (1 - (v - lo) / (hi - lo)) * (H - padT - padB);
      for (let s = -3; s <= 6; s++) {
        mk("line", { x1: X(anchor + s), y1: padT, x2: X(anchor + s), y2: H - padB, stroke: line, "stroke-width": 1 });
        mk("text", { x: X(anchor + s), y: H - 8, "text-anchor": "middle", fill: faint, "font-size": 11, "font-weight": 600 }, s === 0 ? "release" : `${s > 0 ? "+" : ""}${s} s`);
      }
      mk("text", { x: 4, y: Y(hi - 3) + 4, fill: faint, "font-size": 11 }, Math.round(hi - 3));
      mk("text", { x: 4, y: Y(lo + 3) + 4, fill: faint, "font-size": 11 }, Math.round(lo + 3));
      mk("text", { x: 4, y: (padT + H - padB) / 2 + 4, fill: faint, "font-size": 11, "font-weight": 600 }, "red");
      if (crt.ok) {
        mk("line", { x1: padL, y1: Y(crt.y0), x2: W - padR, y2: Y(crt.y0), stroke: faint, "stroke-dasharray": "4 4" });
        mk("line", { x1: padL, y1: Y(crt.yInf), x2: W - padR, y2: Y(crt.yInf), stroke: faint, "stroke-dasharray": "4 4" });
        mk("text", { x: W - padR, y: Y(crt.y0) - 4, "text-anchor": "end", fill: faint, "font-size": 11 }, "pressed: blood squeezed out");
        mk("text", { x: W - padR, y: Y(crt.yInf) + 13, "text-anchor": "end", fill: faint, "font-size": 11 }, "baseline: blood back");
      }
      let d = ""; for (const i of idx) d += (d ? " L" : "M") + X(crt.t[i]).toFixed(1) + "," + Y(crt.sm[i]).toFixed(1);
      mk("path", { d, fill: "none", stroke: accent, "stroke-width": 2.2, "stroke-linejoin": "round" });
      if (crt.ok && crt.t90 != null) {
        const tx = crt.tOn + crt.t90;
        mk("rect", { x: X(crt.tOn), y: padT, width: Math.max(1, X(tx) - X(crt.tOn)), height: H - padT - padB, fill: accent, opacity: 0.1 });
        mk("circle", { cx: X(tx), cy: Y(crt.thr90), r: 4, fill: accent });
        mk("text", { x: X(tx) + 7, y: Y(crt.thr90) + 4, fill: ink, "font-size": 12, "font-weight": 700 }, `90% back at ${crt.t90.toFixed(2)} s`);
      }
    }
    if (crt.ok) {
      el.crt.textContent = `${crt.t90.toFixed(2)} s`;
      el.crtNote.textContent = `Pressed hard for four seconds, then relaxed without lifting. The red level rose by ${crt.amp.toFixed(0)} units while the capillaries were empty and fell back when blood returned. Under two seconds is normal; a nurse counting by eye would call this "under one".`;
    } else {
      el.crt.textContent = "–"; el.crtNote.textContent = `No refill reported: ${crt.reason}.`;
    }
    drawRefill();

    /* ---------- nurse board ---------- */
    let ready = false;
    function updateBoard(unlock) {
      if (unlock) {
        ready = true;
        el.hr2.disabled = el.rr2.disabled = false;
        if (full.hr != null) el.hr2.value = full.hr;
        if (full.rr != null) el.rr2.value = full.rr;
      }
      const flags = complaintFlags(el.complaint.value), pain = Number(el.pain.value);
      el.painOut.textContent = String(pain);
      el.flags.textContent = flags.length ? `Red flags spotted at check-in: ${flags.join(", ")}.` : "No red-flag words in the complaint.";
      if (!ready) {
        const sc = scorePatient({}, {}, flags, pain);
        el.score.textContent = String(sc.score);
        el.reasons.innerHTML = sc.reasons.length ? sc.reasons.map((r) => `<li>${r}</li>`).join("") : `<li class="vigil__muted">Play the recording to add the measured vitals.</li>`;
        el.vitals.innerHTML = `<li class="vigil__muted">Vitals arrive after the finger check.</li>`;
        el.row.classList.toggle("is-hot", sc.score >= 5);
        el.row.classList.toggle("is-warm", sc.score >= 2 && sc.score < 5);
        return;
      }
      const first = { hr: full.hr, rr: full.rr, crt: crt.ok ? Math.round(crt.t90 * 100) / 100 : null, pi: full.pi };
      const hr2 = Number(el.hr2.value), rr2 = Number(el.rr2.value);
      el.hr2Out.textContent = String(hr2); el.rr2Out.textContent = String(rr2);
      const changed = hr2 !== full.hr || rr2 !== full.rr;
      const last = changed ? { ...first, hr: hr2, rr: rr2 } : first;
      const sc = scorePatient(first, last, flags, pain);
      el.score.textContent = String(sc.score);
      el.vitals.innerHTML = [
        `HR <strong>${fmt(last.hr)}</strong>`, `RR <strong>${fmt(last.rr)}</strong>`, `HRV <strong>${fmt(full.rmssd)}</strong> ms`,
        `PI <strong>${fmt(full.pi, 2)}</strong>%`, `refill <strong>${first.crt == null ? "–" : first.crt.toFixed(2)}</strong> s`,
      ].map((v) => `<li>${v}</li>`).join("");
      el.reasons.innerHTML = sc.reasons.length ? sc.reasons.map((r) => `<li>${r}</li>`).join("") : `<li class="vigil__muted">Nothing to flag. Re-check due in 15 minutes.</li>`;
      el.row.classList.toggle("is-hot", sc.score >= 5);
      el.row.classList.toggle("is-warm", sc.score >= 2 && sc.score < 5);
    }
    el.complaint.addEventListener("input", () => updateBoard(false));
    el.pain.addEventListener("input", () => updateBoard(false));
    el.hr2.addEventListener("input", () => updateBoard(false));
    el.rr2.addEventListener("input", () => updateBoard(false));
    root.querySelectorAll("[data-vigil-example]").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => { el.complaint.value = b.dataset.vigilExample; updateBoard(false); }));
    updateBoard(false);
    drawMonitor();
  })();
</script>
